; What a tiny program asks of its system, as two interfaces, each with an
; implementation for each system it runs on (README.md):
;
; - TinyLibSystem.mli, a tool's system: files, directories, processes,
;   the clock. unix/ is it over OCaml's Unix (Linux, macOS);
;   tinykernel/ over tiny-kernel's calls, compiled by tiny-ml.
; - TinyCalls.mli, tiny-kernel's calls themselves, what a graphical
;   program draws and reads its keys with. tinykernel/ is the kernel's
;   (externals, mlsys.c); sdl/ a window's, on the host; stub/ the tests'.
;
; dune builds the host's sides: both are virtual libraries here, their
; implementations in the directories below (tinykernel/ has no dune file:
; only tiny-ml compiles it, TinyKernel/Makefile).

(library
 (name tiny_lib_system)
 (wrapped false)
 (modules TinyLibSystem)
 (virtual_modules TinyLibSystem)
 (default_implementation tiny_lib_system_unix)
 (libraries ix_core fpath caps))

(library
 (name tiny_calls)
 (wrapped false)
 (modules TinyCalls)
 (virtual_modules TinyCalls)
 (default_implementation tiny_calls_stub))
